    {
      "assertion_set_id": "ERC-review-synthesis",
      "assertions": [
        {
          "assertion_id": "aspiration_reasoning",
          "attribute_key": "classification_review_support",
          "raw_value": "Propose naturally_aspirated for the offered ERC 3.6L Pentastar V6 ESS. The MY19 technical guide positively classifies the same marketed family/ESS architecture as naturally aspirated; applicable US guide/specification lineage identifies ERC, its marketed dimensions and trim/body offerings. Induction continuity across these regional implementations is an engineering judgment supported by the combined evidence, not a direct US manufacturer assertion, code-equality proof or inference from absent turbo words alone.",
          "source_context": "Research synthesis; AU p10 and pinned US offering evidence. Human conclusion, not manufacturer text."
        },
        {
          "assertion_id": "electrification_reasoning",
          "attribute_key": "classification_review_support",
          "raw_value": "Propose none for the ten offered ERC configurations. US manual hardware descriptions distinguish conventional ESS starting equipment from an eTorque motor-generator with hybrid battery and launch assistance; the MY2019 catalog positively identifies conventional without-eTorque alternator applications and a separate ERG BSG application. US offering lineage binds the ten rows to ERC ESS; contemporary MY2020 powertrain materials separately introduce/describe V6 eTorque Sahara. The combined architecture/applicability judgment requires human adjudication; neither ESS terminology, missing eTorque words nor introduction chronology alone establishes nonhybrid status.",
          "source_context": "Research synthesis; US manual hardware, catalog applications and MY2020 press context."
        },
        {
          "assertion_id": "scope_limitations",
          "attribute_key": "classification_review_support",
          "raw_value": "No explicit US ERC naturally aspirated/nonhybrid statement was found. Australian-to-US induction continuity and the ERC conventional-hardware association are derived. Catalog provenance and MY2020 introduction chronology are not conclusive alone. Regulatory material and retrospective FCA Y40 also describe MY2019 3.6L hybrid/eTorque applications without establishing that they are ERC; the proposal is restricted to the ten retained ERC offerings, not all MY2019 3.6L Wranglers.",
          "source_context": "All limitations must remain visible to the human reviewer."
        }
      ],
      "extraction_mode": "manually_verified_transcription",
